{%- comment -%}
  Licensed webfont declarations, rendered inline in <head> (see
  layout/theme.liquid). This has to be a snippet rather than a linked
  stylesheet: Shopify's CDN serves files in /assets as raw static files, so
  a linked "fonts.css.liquid" never gets its {{ }} tags processed and the
  browser aborts the request. Rendering it as a snippet runs it through
  Liquid before it hits the page, so the asset_url lookups below resolve
  correctly.

  Upload the three .woff2 files to Assets (Edit code > Assets > Add a new
  asset, or drop them in this theme's /assets folder and `shopify theme
  push`). If your filenames differ, update the asset_url calls below to
  match exactly — Shopify asset URLs are case-sensitive.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'OT Neue Montreal';
    src: url('{{ 'OTNeueMontreal-BoldSqueezed.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Neue Haas Grotesk Text Pro';
    src: url('{{ 'NeueHaasGroteskTextPro-55Roman.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Neue Haas Grotesk Text Pro';
    src: url('{{ 'NeueHaasGroteskTextPro-65Medium.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
</style>
